# Files that run on the Linux droplet must keep LF line endings, whatever the
# machine they are committed from (decisions §46, pass 2): Git on Windows may
# convert text files to CRLF in the working copy, and a shell script with CRLF
# fails on Linux ("set: Illegal option -"), as do systemd unit files. `eol=lf`
# makes Git write these with LF everywhere.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
